</div>
```

#### CSS:

```css
.emotion-container {
    margin: 20px;
}

.happy-thumb, .sad-thumb {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 10px;
    margin: 10px;
    cursor: pointer;
    background-color: #f0c040;
    border-radius: 5px;
    text-align: center;
}

.popup {
    display: none;
    position: fixed;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    padding: 20px;
    background-color: white;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
    z-index: 1000;
}

.popup.show {
    display: block;
}

.close {
    cursor: pointer;
    float: right;
    font-size: 24px;
}
```

#### JavaScript:

```javascript
function togglePopup(popupId) {
    // Close any open popups
    const popups = document.querySelectorAll('.popup');
    popups.forEach(function(popup) {
        popup.classList.remove('show');
    });

    // Show the selected popup
    const popup = document.getElementById(popupId);
    popup.classList.toggle("show");
}

function closePopup(popupId) {
    const popup = document.getElementById(popupId);
    popup.classList.remove("show");
}
```

### Key Points:

1. **Popup Visibility**: The popups are hidden by default (using `display: none;`) and are set to `display: block;` when the class `show` is added.

2. **CSS Class Toggle**: The `togglePopup` function ensures that all other popups are closed before showing the selected one to improve user experience.

3. **Close Functionality**: Each popup has a close button (×) which allows users to easily close the popup.

